        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Example 2 as shown in Figure H.6 shows example 1 of the certificate structure but with the vehicle certificate chain cross signed by the V2G root CA certificate. This allows the SECC to validate the vehicle certificate using the V2G root CA certificate during TLS session setup. The SECC does not need OEM root CA certificate to validate the vehicle certificate.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                217,
